title: '[WIP] cumulus: fix V3 scheduling parent picking, wait for RC tip'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: "# Description\n\nStacked on #13163.\n\nAt rpo 0 the V3 scheduling\
    \ parent is the last finished-slot relay block, which may have same-height siblings\
    \ \u2014 picking among them from the local view is arrival-order luck, and building\
    \ on the losing sibling wastes the slot. Like the V2 path, the collator now waits\
    \ for a relay block of the current production slot: its parent hash names the\
    \ canonical finished-height block.\nThis trades a little slot time (normally milliseconds)\
    \ for fork-safe scheduling parents and ties parachain block production to the\
    \ relay chain cadence.\n\nThe walk-back is also bounded by the slot-timer's production\
    \ slot instead of a second wall-clock read. The principle here is that the slot\
    \ timer is the source of truth for the current slot."
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: patch
